{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Haman fell.</b> For he was pleading and bowing at her feet, and when he saw that the king's wrath returned, he fell from his great terror. And the way of derash is well known." "<b>To overpower the queen.</b> A euphemism for lying down, that she would be under his authority; and behold, he would force her. Like it: וכבשוה (and overpowered her). And the meaning of 'my people' [is] that I have seen this." "<b>Covered.</b> The attendants. And the meaning is like 'his face,' for such is the custom of the kings of Persia, that the servants of the king cover the face of one against whom the king is angry, so that the king will not see him again. And this is already well known in the books of Persia."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:13.516078641Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}